@startuml
title Download Data Flow
skinparam shadowing false

start
group HTTP layer
  :POST /api/jobs with url + DownloadOptions;
  :extract_metadata (with cookies when present);
  :insert Job and one JobItem per selected entry;
  :enqueue queued JobItem ids;
end group

group JobManager
  :worker dequeues an item id;
  :claim lock: check status, set running, commit;
  :offload to a thread via asyncio.to_thread;
  :prepare_download resolves the planned format and size;
end group

group yt-dlp
  :build_download_options for the profile chain;
  :extract and download, emit progress payloads;
  if (media stream failure?) then (yes)
    :try the next profile;\nDownloadStalled and Cancel skip the chain;
  else (no)
  endif
end group

group progress pipeline
  :DownloadProgressAggregator merges substreams;
  :TransferStats records bytes and elapsed time;
  :StallGuard checks whether the byte peak advanced;
  if (peak stale for the timeout?) then (yes)
    :raise DownloadStalled, item fails visibly;
    stop
  else (no)
  endif
  :ProgressPersistGate decides write vs skip;
end group

group persistence and UI
  :update JobItem, then aggregate the Job row;
  :append a JobEvent row and publish on EventBroker;
  :SSE message reaches the browser;
  :GET /api/jobs reads the job_read_model projection;
  :React task center renders the new state;
end group
stop

note right
The gate throttles writes (>=250ms, or >=0.5% progress,
or a terminal status), so five parallel workers do not
turn every chunk callback into a commit.
end note
@enduml
